            0.129,
            0.055,
            0.55,
            0.073
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "§6. The Fourier Transform and Differentiation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.835,
            0.056,
            0.871,
            0.071
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "335"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.099,
            0.248,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "for f in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { D } _ { \\alpha }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.125,
            0.723,
            0.22
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_349_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{align*}\\int_{-a}^{a} f \\bar{h} &= \\overline{H(a)} f(a) - \\overline{H(-a)} f(-a) - \\int_{-a}^{a} f' \\bar{H} \\\\&= - \\int_{-a}^{a} f' \\bar{H}.\\end{align*}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.227,
            0.87,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\int _ { - a } ^ { a } f ^ { \\prime } [ \\bar { H } - ( \\bar { \\imath } \\bar { g } ) ] = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for every f in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { D } _ { a ^ { \\cdot } } \\mathbf { A } \\mathbf { s }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in (1.11), it follows that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "H - i g"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is coñstant on "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "[ - a , a ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and g is absolutely continuous. Moreover, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 = H ^ { \\prime } - i g ^ { \\prime } = h - i g ^ { \\prime } ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "A^{*}g = h =ig^{\\prime}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g \\in \\mathcal { D }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and A is self-adjoint."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.285,
            0.871,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If A is the differentiation operator in Example 6.1, what is the group "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "U ( t ) = \\exp ( i t A ) ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Since A is not represented as a multiplication operator, Proposition 5.16 cannot be applied. One could proceed to try and discover the spectral measure for A. Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "A = \\int x d E ( x ) , U ( t ) = \\int e ^ { i t x } d E ( x )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Or one could be clever."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.376,
            0.871,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Later in this section it will be shown that if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { F } \\colon L ^ { 2 } ( \\mathbb { R } ) \\to L ^ { 2 } ( \\mathbb { R } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the Fourier-Plancherel transform, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { F }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a unitary operator (6.17) and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal{F}^{-1} A \\mathcal{F} ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the operator on "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { 2 } ( \\mathbb { R } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of multiplication by the independent variable (6.18). Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { F } ^ { - 1 } U ( t ) \\mathcal { F }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is multiplication by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "e ^ { i x t } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " But it is possible to find U(t) directly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.469,
            0.394,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall that if f ∈dom A,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.384,
            0.496,
            0.614,
            0.539
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_349_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "A f = - i \\lim _ { t \\rightarrow 0 } \\frac { U ( t ) f - f } { t }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.538,
            0.163,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.554,
            0.65,
            0.596
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_349_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "f^{\\prime}(x)=\\lim_{t \\to 0}-\\frac{(U(t)f)(x)-f(x)}{t}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.605,
            0.673,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Being clever, one might guess that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( U ( t ) f ) ( x ) = f ( x - t )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.64,
            0.872,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.2. Theorem. If A and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { D }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are as in Example 6.1 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "U ( t ) = \\exp ( i t A )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( U ( t ) f ) ( x ) = f ( x - t )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for all f in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { 2 } ( \\mathbb { R } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and x,t in R."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.686,
            0.873,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "PROOF. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(V(t)f)(x) = f(x - t)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . It is easy to see that V is a strongly continuous one parameter unitary group. Let B be the infinitesimal generator of V. It must be shown that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "B = A"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.739,
            0.873,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that f ∈dom B if and only if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\operatorname* { l i m } _ { t \\to 0 } t ^ { - 1 } ( V ( t ) f - f )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " exists. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f   \\in   \\mathsf { C } _ { c } ^ { ( 1 ) } ( \\mathbb { R } ) ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that is, f is continuously differentiable and has compact support. Thus for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t > 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.802,
            0.753,
            0.847
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_349_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\left[ \\frac{V(t)f - f}{t} \\right](x) = \\frac{f(x - t) - f(x)}{t} = - \\frac{1}{t} \\int_{x - t}^{x} f'(y)dy"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.847,
            0.174,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.217,
            0.872,
            0.778,
            0.947
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_349_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\left| \\frac{V(t)f(x) - f(x)}{t} + f^{\\prime}(x) \\right| & \\leqslant \\frac{1}{t} \\int_{x - t}^{x} \\left| f^{\\prime}(x) - f^{\\prime}(y) \\right| dy \\\\& \\leqslant \\sup \\left\\{ \\left| f^{\\prime}(x) - f^{\\prime}(y) \\right| : |x - y| \\leqslant t \\right\\}.\\end{aligned}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
